# Orchestration

`WORKFLOW.md` is the control-plane contract. Do not invent Linear statuses.

- Dispatch only when status is `Backlog`, the issue is delegated to Cursor, and it has no `blockedBy`.
- Claim by moving to `Implementing` before code changes.
- One issue → one branch from `development` → one PR into `development`.
- Nick moving the issue to `Done` is merge approval. Then `/land`.
- Never push to `staging` or `production` from an issue land run.
- Runtime agents use Linear MCP. They must not create teams or workflow states.
- Domain sub-agents are helpers inside `/implement`. They do not get their own Linear issues.
